# UPDOWNLY — Complete Build Specification for Claude Code

You are building **UPDOWNLY**, a premium-feeling, installable iOS PWA trivia game built around one addictive question:

**Is the next number higher or lower?**

This is a new application built from scratch. It is not a reskin of another game. Use the design principles, engineering discipline, iOS polish, offline-first architecture and attention to detail described in this brief to deliver a genuinely finished product.

The game should feel like a small, carefully designed App Store game, not a website squeezed onto an iPhone.

The core gameplay is simple enough for anyone to understand within five seconds. The depth comes from its thousands of real facts, dozens of categories, increasingly difficult comparisons, personal records and replayability.

**Do not stop at a plan, mock-up or basic prototype. Build the working application, populate the data, test the game and polish the finished experience.**

Do not ask me questions. Make sensible decisions, document significant choices in `DECISIONS.md` and keep working until the definition of done is satisfied.

