# 14. Testing requirements

Testing is part of the implementation, not a final optional step.

## 14.1 Unit tests

At minimum, cover:

### Fact data

- Unique IDs.
- Provenance requirements.
- Valid numeric values.
- Valid metric definitions.
- Dataset record counts.
- Compatible comparison groups.
- Duplicate detection.
- Unit consistency.
- Period consistency.
- Correct numeric formatting.

### Game engine

- Higher answer is correct when appropriate.
- Lower answer is correct when appropriate.
- Incorrect answers register correctly.
- Equal values never produce ambiguous questions.
- Missing and invalid facts are excluded.
- A question cannot score twice.
- Streaks update correctly.
- Classic ends after an incorrect answer.
- Sprint continues after an incorrect answer.
- Sprint finishes on time.
- Daily mode contains exactly ten questions.
- Daily sequences are reproducible.
- A new daily date produces the intended new sequence.
- No immediate duplicate comparisons.
- No infinite loops on small or exhausted pools.
- Scoring remains correct when answers are tapped rapidly.

### Persistence

- Scores survive reloads.
- Settings survive reloads.
- Corrupt storage does not crash the app.
- Unavailable storage degrades gracefully.
- Resetting statistics clears the relevant data.
- Best scores do not decrease accidentally.

## 14.2 End-to-end tests

Use Playwright with a mobile viewport and realistic touch interactions.

Test:

1. Open the app and start Quick Play.
2. Select a category and difficulty.
3. Complete a correct comparison.
4. Complete an incorrect comparison.
5. Verify scores and streaks.
6. Play multiple questions in succession.
7. End a Classic round.
8. Complete a Sprint round with a controllable test clock.
9. Complete a Daily Challenge.
10. Verify daily result persistence.
11. Open Stats and verify updated records.
12. Change settings.
13. Reset data.
14. Navigate away from and back to a running game safely.
15. Handle fast, repeated taps.
16. Verify there are no console errors.
17. Verify the app works under a GitHub Pages subpath.
18. Load the app, disconnect the network and play using bundled data.
19. Test light and dark themes.
20. Test narrow screens, long item names and unusually large values.

Use a deterministic dataset and seeded randomness in automated tests. Do not make tests depend on live external APIs.

## 14.3 Visual review

Capture and inspect screenshots at approximately:

- 390 × 844.
- 375 × 812.
- 844 × 390 for desktop/mobile landscape resilience.
- A larger desktop viewport.

Review:

- Play screen.
- Category browser.
- Category details.
- Active question.
- Correct answer reveal.
- Incorrect answer reveal.
- Results.
- Daily Challenge.
- Stats.
- Settings.
- Data source information.
- Installation help.
- Empty or error states.

Review in light and dark modes.

Fix actual layout issues. Do not merely generate screenshots and declare success.

Save the final screenshots in `design/screens/`.

